The initial Pi desktop-wrapper architecture was inspired by Picot:
https://github.com/shixin-guo/picot

ZiCode Studio Desktop was not directly forked from Picot and does not track its
development. According to the maintainer's historical account, Picot was a fork
of Tau (https://github.com/deflating/tau). Picot's original public URL is no longer
accessible as of 2026-10-10; its historical fork metadata cannot be reverified.
Tau is retired. Retained repository history and compatibility identifiers do not
imply ongoing synchronization or wholly original authorship. Existing MIT
copyright notices remain in LICENSE and relevant source files.

Bundled third-party runtimes keep their own licenses:

- Pi: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
- Git for Windows / PortableGit: https://gitforwindows.org/
- Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime:
  https://developer.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/webview2/

Release builds download pinned official artifacts and verify their SHA-256
digests. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/windows-packaging.md.
